      "writtenOn": "2023-03-13T17:10:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e please use your own ioctl type, not a custom one.\n\nI don\u0027t want to conflict with upstream ioctl numbers. If I pick 0x6 (arbitrary), then upstream can never use 0x6 which will look odd due to downstream usage of that number. Using separate ioctl type that would never be submitted upstream lets me avoid this conflict.\n\n\u003e and why start at 0x10?\n\nNo particular reason to start at 0x10.",
